lso money-heavy on this side      / dropped if the consensus is money-heavy the OTHER way\n    + line move toward this side since the open      (+4/pt spread, +3/pt total, +100 x implied-prob for ML)\n      ... and the same penalty when it moved away     (reverse line movement against the side)\n    + model edge in this side's direction            (x sport weight: the models with a track record count more)\n  Out: thin markets (DK 100/0), moneylines outside -250..+300 (one big ticket on a longshot isn't \"sharp\"),\n  games already started, and games whose own flags point opposite ways (ML one side, spread the other).\n  One pick per game (correlated legs are one bet). Qualify at score >= SCORE_MIN; take 3-10.\n  Units: 10% 5U / 20% 4U / 30% 3U / 30% 2U / 10% 1U with minimums 1/1/2/2/1, filled from the top so a\n  short slate drops the 1U and 2U tiers first.\n\nYAK'S LOTTOS (0.25U, about 4-10 a day, only if they price as +EV)\n  Moneylines from +750 to +4000. Our model's win probability is shrunk toward the no-vig book price\n  (long-shot tails are where models are least trustworthy) and the pick needs EV >= LOTTO_EV_MIN after\n  that. No padding: a day with two +EV long shots gets two. (Alt spreads: no priced feed available yet.)\n\nLOCK + GRADING\n  The day's card is built at the first build on or after LOCK_HOUR PT and never changes afterwards (games\n  that started before the lock are skipped). Every build grades finished picks from the sports' own\n  results, at the price taken, and records closing-line value from the ledgers.\n"}